  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "Which of the following numbers is largest?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(9.12344 \\)",
    "B": "\\(9.123\\overline{4} \\)",
    "C": "\\(9.12\\overline{34} \\)",
    "D": "\\(9.1\\overline{234} \\)",
    "E": "\\(9.\\overline{1234} \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "A bar means that the marked digits repeat forever. Append zeros to the terminating decimal so that the choices can be compared place by place:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nA&=9.12344000\\ldots,\\\\\nB&=9.12344444\\ldots,\\\\\nC&=9.12343434\\ldots,\\\\\nD&=9.12342342\\ldots,\\\\\nE&=9.12341234\\ldots.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nAll five agree through the first four decimal places. At the fifth decimal place, \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) have \\(4\\), while \\(C,D,E\\) have \\(3,2,1\\), respectively. Thus the largest must be \\(A\\) or \\(B\\). At the sixth decimal place, \\(B\\) has \\(4\\) and \\(A\\) has \\(0\\). Therefore the largest number is \\(9.123\\overline4\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
